    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26681" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĕālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		linea, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>consisting of lines, made with lines, lineal</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambitus lineales,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 16, 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĕālĭter</span></b> , <i>in the manner of lines, by means of lines</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quos (circulos) linealiter feci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 8, § 834</span></i>
			.</div>
